-- #1111 A-2.6, the severity mirror's SHARPEST cell: #1256's exact collision graph,
-- but with a genuinely wrong field value.
--
-- A-2.6 makes the overlay pick `arcol.Cfg` (`fld : Int`).  It must then REJECT
-- `fld = "s"` — `String vs Int`.  What must NOT happen is acceptance by falling
-- through to `zrcol.Cfg`, whose `fld : Float` is equally wrong for a String but whose
-- presence is the whole reason the old lookup was ambiguous; nor may the two
-- candidate records be silently unified into something that accepts both.
--
-- This is the cell that distinguishes "the overlay picked the right record" from
-- "the overlay made record-literal checking permissive".  The drain fixtures cannot
-- see the difference: they only assert that a CORRECT literal is accepted.
import arcol.{Cfg}
import zrcol.{zrf}

bad : Cfg
bad = Cfg { fld = "s" }

main : <IO> Unit
main = println (zrf 1)
